PLAN: what to explore next
==========================

No budget is committed. Each item needs the person's yes on its cost before it runs. Costs are
estimates at the rates measured on 2026-10-19, about this much per agent wake:
  Opus     about $0.12
  Sonnet   about $0.06
  Haiku    under $0.01
  Fable    about $0.29

Fable was about 60% of every swarm's cost. A mix of Opus, Sonnet and Haiku keeps model
difference for far less. Fable can be kept for when its difference is the point.

What the runs so far suggest about cost
  The baseline (runs\2026-10-19-baseline) found that one Opus taking up four seeds wrote a rule
  as good as or better than R2's 30-wake field. The field's distinct gain was the protections
  that came from being objected to. So most items below use a lighter shape: a seeded draft, one
  real round of objections or checks, and a change. The fuller circle is kept for where a
  circle is the thing being tested.


A. Owed from earlier runs (small)
---------------------------------
  A1  Re-check R4's corrected reading, and R2's corrected reading.
      One Haiku or Sonnet wake each. About $0.10. Closes two "not re-checked" notes.
  A2  Replay R5's record checks (practices\aggregate, "Checks on the record") on R2's ledger,
      where no one was playing a counterfeit, and count false alarms.
      One Sonnet wake. About $0.06. Tests the "discerning" variant and CRITIQUE 4.


A+. Token levers, tested cheaply (MAP, "The economics of signal")
-----------------------------------------------------------------
  L1  Harness weight. The same short wake run three ways: a default general-purpose agent, an
      agent with only Read and Write, and a continued agent rather than a fresh one. Compare
      tokens per wake. Haiku. Under $0.05. Measures the biggest single cost found so far.
  L2  Read the outcome, store the ledger. Give a fresh Haiku voice R2's corrected reading and
      outcome only, plus permission to open record.txt by entry number. Ask it to check one claim. Count what
      it read. About $0.01. Tests whether checkability survives without reading everything.

B. The lighter shape, tested directly
-------------------------------------
  B1  Seeded draft, then objections, then a change. Same task as R2. One Opus seeded draft,
      three objectors (Sonnet, Haiku, Haiku), and one change. Judged blind against R2 and B2.
      About $0.50. Answers: can the field's protections be had at low cost?


C. Types not yet practised (MAP)
--------------------------------
  C1  Resonant: a pair works closely, then harvests to a third voice (the tuning forks; the
      campfire). About $0.40.
  C2  Fractal: two circles on two parts of one question, harvesting to a trunk reading (the
      watershed; the tree). About $0.80.
  C3  Reparative: needs a repair practice first (writing it costs nothing). A staged, consented
      harm in a short run, plus a first draft of harm determination (tension 4) (kintsugi).
      About $0.60.
  C4  Synthetic, done as the meeting of waters: two seeds run side by side for two steps
      without mixing, then merge. Compare with mixing at once. About $0.40.
  C5  Narrative, done as sourdough: one practice passes through three short fields in turn,
      each revising it, and the lineages are compared. About $0.60.


D. Candidate types from images (IMAGES, part 2)
-----------------------------------------------
  D1  Braided (the rope): a relay of 6-8 short wakes with a two-hand-off overlap, with and
      without counter-twisted seeds. About $0.50 on Sonnet and Haiku.
  D2  Releasing (ants): a board with no rounds where entries fade unless cited. Watch for an
      ant mill. Needs a small script for the fading; writing it costs nothing. About $0.50.
  D3  Threshold (bees): three options, five voices, a quorum of three independent checks, set
      beside R4's tally. About $0.60.
  D4  Neighbourly (the murmuration): six voices in a ring, each reading two neighbours. How far
      does one strong claim travel? About $0.40.
  D5  Fallow: the same task twice, once with a voice-called rest built in (any voice may pause
      the field for one wake, and the field must not fill it). Does anything change? About
      $0.60.
  D6  Kindred (lichen): a field with another provider's model. Waits on what the firm's IT
      policy allows. Nothing here closes that door.


